{
  "$comment": "Gold-standard prerequisite pairs. relation 'requires' means a is a hard prerequisite of b; 'unrelated' means no direct learning-structure relation. Objective domain facts only — no taste judgements. `lang` is the BCP-47 tag the pair is written in: the edge judge reads a label plus a one-line summary, and both have to be in one language for the judgement to mean anything.\nSources: the zh-CN pairs are hand-authored by Fable 5 (2026-08-01). The nine other language sets are hand-authored (2026-09-07) — direction is a structural claim, so it is not delegated to a model — with every concept label cross-checked, where the extraction covers it, against the Wiktionary-derived term index in scripts/language-packs/.cache/interlingua/*.json (Wiktionary via kaikki.org, CC BY-SA 4.0). Verified this way: hi भिन्न/प्रायिकता/बीजगणित/ज्यामिति/त्रिकोणमिति, bn সীমা/বীজগণিত/সম্ভাবনা, ru функция/уравнение/дробь/вероятность/предел, ar معادلة/نهاية/احتمال, id pecahan/variabel/fungsi, es fracción/probabilidad/límite, ja 変数/関数/確率, ko 확률/분수, en all. Terms the extraction has no row for (mostly the calculus and CS vocabulary, which Wiktionary covers thinly outside English) are the standard school/university terms and were reviewed by hand.\nWhy more than Chinese: goldBaseline is the only judge that measures the edge judge against documented truth, and until 2026-09-07 it could only ever measure it in Chinese.",
